{#
  Adverse action notice, ECOA / Regulation B section 1002.9.

  Generated from the LEDGER ROW, never from a live re-score, so the letter always
  states the decision that was actually recorded. Content follows 1002.9(a)(2):
  statement of the action taken, the creditor's identity, the ECOA notice verbatim,
  the administering agency, and the specific principal reasons.

  The FCRA disclosures are deliberately absent and the absence is explained — see the
  final paragraph. Including inapplicable boilerplate would be worse than omitting it.
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Notice of Action Taken — {{ decision_id }}</title>
<style>{{ fonts_css }}</style>
<style>{{ pack_css }}</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="banner">
  Demonstration artifact &mdash; generated by a reference implementation &mdash; not a legal notice
</div>

<div class="letterhead">
  <div class="name">{{ issuer.creditor_name }}</div>
  <div class="addr">{{ issuer.creditor_address }}</div>
</div>

<div class="meta">
  {{ notice_date }}<br>
  Application reference: <span class="mono">{{ decision_id }}</span>
</div>

<h1>Notice of action taken on your credit application</h1>

<p>
  Thank you for your recent application for a mortgage loan to purchase a home. After
  reviewing the information provided with your application, we are unable to approve
  your request at this time.
</p>

<h2>Principal reasons for our decision</h2>

<p>
  The Equal Credit Opportunity Act requires us to tell you the specific principal
  reasons for this decision. They are:
</p>

<ol class="reasons">
  {% for r in reason_codes %}
  <li>{{ r.text }}.</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>

{% if counterfactual and counterfactual.achievable %}
<h2>What would have changed the outcome</h2>
<div class="counterfactual">{{ counterfactual.sentence }}</div>
<p style="font-size:9pt;color:var(--muted)">
  This describes how our assessment would have differed if that single factor had been
  different and everything else had stayed the same. In practice these factors move
  together, so it is an illustration of how your application was assessed rather than
  a guarantee about a future application.
</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Your rights under federal law</h2>

<div class="statute">
  <p>
    The federal Equal Credit Opportunity Act prohibits creditors from discriminating
    against credit applicants on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin,
    sex, marital status, age (provided the applicant has the capacity to enter into a
    binding contract); because all or part of the applicant's income derives from any
    public assistance program; or because the applicant has in good faith exercised any
    right under the Consumer Credit Protection Act.
  </p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:0">
    The federal agency that administers compliance with this law concerning this
    creditor is the {{ issuer.federal_agency_name }}, {{ issuer.federal_agency_address }}.
  </p>
</div>

<p>
  If you have questions about this decision, or would like to discuss your
  application, please contact us at the address above.
</p>

<h2>Consumer report information</h2>

<p>
  <strong>No consumer report or credit score was used in reaching this decision.</strong>
  Our assessment was based solely on the application information described above.
  Because no consumer report was obtained, the disclosures that the Fair Credit
  Reporting Act would otherwise require &mdash; the notice under section 615(a) that
  a consumer report was used, and the credit score disclosure under section 609(g)
  &mdash; do not apply and are deliberately omitted rather than included as
  inapplicable boilerplate.
</p>

<div class="audit">
  <dl>
    <dt>Decision reference</dt><dd class="mono">{{ decision_id }}</dd>
    <dt>Recorded</dt><dd>{{ created_at }}</dd>
    <dt>Model version</dt><dd>{{ model_version }}</dd>
    <dt>Model hash</dt><dd class="mono">{{ model_hash }}</dd>
    <dt>Ledger position</dt><dd>{{ ledger_seq }}</dd>
    <dt>Ledger row hash</dt><dd class="mono">{{ row_hash }}</dd>
    <dt>Chain status at issue</dt><dd>{{ chain_status }}</dd>
  </dl>
</div>

</body>
</html>
